A||||20||GREENDANO||Guess What I did yesterday?||||10||
Z||000000||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||03:26 PM||||I pulled the V8 out of my F40 to rebuild the tranny and freshen the engine.  The builder of this car let the car sit for many years, and it was never on the road with the V8.  From my expirience in finding little surprises as I dig into this car, I decided to yank the powertrain and rebuild the tranny so it doesn't explode on it's maiden voyage.<BR>  Dan-O<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/WorkingDanO.JPG"> <p>[This message has been edited by GREENDANO (edited 01-09-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||03:29 PM||||I've tried three times, and my picture won't post.  <BR>  Maybe later it will.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||13
Z||000002||batboy||01-09-2000||04:55 PM||||Dan-o, it's the spaces in the image file name. To post it that way, you can't use any spaces. Tell us how you are going to built the engine, or do you even know yet?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||01-09-2000||05:30 PM||||I changed the spaces to underscores and edited your message, hope you don't mind Dan. The forum software doesn't understand spaces inside a URL, that's why it didn't work.||||reg||7
Z||000005||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||05:47 PM||||I reposted it without the spaces...That did the trick.  Thanks for the tip Batboy and Cliff, I never mind help!!  <BR>Notice the coolant gushing from the water pump area.  Man, what a mess!  Cleaned my mess today and got the powertrain out of the cradle.  Trans is ready to go to work tomorrow morning, our tranny guy where I work is going to help me.  <BR>  Batboy, I'm not sure yet on the engine.  I think I might re-gasket it and give it a Rustoleum rebuild.  What are ya, scarred?  That's a little V8 Fiero humor for you.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">~ Considering what I drive in the summer, I suppose a radical motor was in order like my pro streeter, I want to be able to pass a gas station.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Supposedly the motor is fresh,It's just been sitting for almost eight years from what I can gather from paperwork I got and the past owner.<BR>  BTW, I'm VERY glad I took the motor out!!!!!!!!!  I found one of the torque converter bolts hand tight!  There's that kaboom I was avoiding.<BR>  Dan-O<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Taillessrear.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||10:24 PM||||Greendano--What happens if someone slams your door?  Will the roof cave in or something?  Just curious as you seem to be very adamant about it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000007||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||11:41 PM||||An unfortunate incident with the wife made that little note necessary.  I was painting a car one day.  Wifey was out visiting in the shop.  It was windy that day and when she left the door flew open.  No big deal.  So rather than leave quietly, or closing the door normally, she slammed it against the wind.  REALLY HARD!!  Do you see the all the stuff on the wall?  All that fell down on me and the car I was woking on.  Not only did I have to repaint the part that got hit, I had to do body work besides.  Kind-of ate up the profits.  I'm not a ****  in any way, that's actually a joke.  When people come over, I love their reaction.<BR>  DO NOT SLAM!!!<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||11
Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-10-2000||05:31 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">I was kinda joking about it, but I can see your point!||||reg||1
Z||000009||mshill||01-12-2000||06:47 PM||||Dan-O,  I just got my V6 out last night.  After muscling loose the last cradle bolt (drivers side rear) with a 1/2 inch ratchet and a 2ft pipe extension, I was able to singlehandedly raise the car with two floor jacks and rolled out the cradle on a pair of furniture dollys.  My wife (I told her to come watch the last five minutes) was freaking out cause the back end of the car was so high in the air.<P>It was about 10pm and it was all I could do to keep myself from starting in and ripping off the accessories (starter, alternator, etc.).||||reg||1
Z||000010||GREENDANO||01-12-2000||10:54 PM||||Whatya' got planned for the motor?  Anything good?  Maybe a 3.2 comnersion....<BR>  Hey BaaaatBoyyyyy....I'm still gonna catch you.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>  Dan-O||||reg||5
Z||000011||batboy||01-13-2000||12:08 PM||||I don't care if other Fieros (or even Fiero based kit cars) can beat the Batmobile. As long as I can still beat the rice burners.||||reg||1
Z||000012||GREENDANO||01-13-2000||09:07 PM||||I'm just teasing...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> Plus, you can look good in the car you're beating them with.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
Z||000013||mshill||01-13-2000||09:50 PM||||Dan-O,  this one stays pretty much stock.  I do have a cam that is going in it.  It is getting new rings, main/rod/cam bearings, timing set, valve job, manifold work (I found  cracks in both), clutch, struts and performance springs.  What prompted me to pull the engine was that I have a clogged muffler.  So, I will be getting new cat back too.<P>I was taking stuff off today.  Broke one manifold bolt  and one of the bolts from the crossover to the front manifold is stripped and will have to be cut off.  Other than that it is going OK.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||GREENDANO||01-14-2000||06:09 PM||||Sounds good.  I'm curious as to why your not pursuing a 3.1/3.2 conversion.  You can have more power but still keep stock appearances.  The only price difference is the crank, dampner and flywheel.  Things that at least I was replacing anyway.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||10
Z||000015||DRH||01-14-2000||06:40 PM||||mshill, <BR>A small torch will save you untold grief when trying to remove bolts that have been in 12+ years. I bought a small propane/oxygen one that uses the small bottles for about $30 including the first bottle of each. Just heat the bolt nice and red before removing. Works especially well on thru bolts when you can get to the threads on the back side. Also, very good for steel bolts screwed into aluminum (these tend to get virtually welded together without heat).<P>David.||||reg||1
Z||000016||mshill||01-14-2000||06:40 PM||||Dan-O,  I am under the impression that you also need to replace the pistons (pin location) and fuel pressure regulator as well.  The crank and flywheel alone are pretty expensive.  When I am done I will still only have an 86SE.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Eric||01-14-2000||08:25 PM||||That's true, the pistons must go.  If you start asking yourself, "Why not do this?  Why not do that?" you'll end up spending a bunch more money than you set out to.  Same thing happened to me.<P>Batboy, I think you should give up on your quest to beat the riceburners.  I saw a drag race on ESPN2 where the slowest of the Hondas, Toyotas, etc., were running 12's.  Don't ask what the fastest were running.  What I saw today will make me think twice about engaging that little Civic in the lane next to me in race.  How much horsepower will you get from your new engine???||||reg||1
Z||000018||GREENDANO||01-15-2000||09:59 AM||||I guess converting to a 3.2 is for someone that's completely rebuilding the motor. You would have to buy new pistons anyway, and if you have to machine your crank, that costs money.  It's really not that much more money than what it takes to recon a normal high miler 2.8L  <BR>  Speed costs....How fast can you aford to go?<BR>  ||||reg||5
Z||000019||batboy||01-15-2000||03:58 PM||||My new Z-28 hydraulic roller cam 350 (+0.030) engine with alumunim heads should put out well over 400 HP. Figuring the total vehicle weight to be about 3,000 lbs with driver and fuel, my 1/4 mile calculator puts the Batmobile into the low to mid 11's with this combination. Bring on those riceburners.<P>Actually, to be realistic, with an automatic and street tires, I'd be tickled pink if I could break into the 12's. I'll find out this spring. Heartland Park Dragstrip opens up again in late March. It's only $7 on grudge night to run as many trials as you have time for, depending on how many others are in line too. You can also mutually choice opponents. The dragstrip is literally next door to where I work.<P>I'm going to run some baseline 1/4 mile times with the tired old V8 first and then install the new bad-boy engine. Wait until the rings get seated, then run it a few times to compare times. I hope it'll be worth the three thousand bucks I'll be spending.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 01-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Monkeyman||01-15-2000||06:23 PM||||A "bad-boy" for the batboy.  Hey!  That's catchy!||||reg||1
